source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A table cell reads the control with no space after the `.` as well, and Jira renders the heading inside the cell; a GFM cell holds inline content only, so jiro keeps the text and warns.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|h1.y|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><h1><a name="y"></a>y</h1></td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
| h |
| --- |
| h1.y |
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 2,
    "Construct": "table",
    "Reason": "Jira renders a heading inside this table cell; JFM keeps its text"
  }
]
